Add Generate Invoices (payment capturing) and login throttling (v0.100)

Generate Invoices:
- New INVOICE_PENDING order status: a fully-despatched order on a company
  (credit) account now lands here instead of going straight to Complete,
  and sits on a new Invoicing > Generate Invoices page until picked up.
  An order with no company (already paid at checkout) still goes straight
  to Complete as before.
- Generate Invoices page: pick a Generation Date and Invoice/Credit, tick
  the order lines to include (or Select all), Generate. Selection is per
  order LINE rather than per order, so one order's lines can be split
  across separate invoices (e.g. phones vs routers) per the customer's
  own preference.
- Generating builds a PDF matching the current OrderWise invoice layout,
  allocates the next invoice/credit note number (one shared sequence,
  continuing from OrderWise's own numbering and editable from Settings),
  emails it to the company's Invoice Email with a saved local copy, and
  marks the order Complete once every line on it has been invoiced.
- Credit notes (from processed RMAs) flow through the same page and the
  same INVOICE_PENDING mechanism, under the Credit radio button.
- New per-company settings (Companies): Invoice Email, a VAT rate override
  (e.g. 0% for a zero-rated Irish account), and Invoice Grouping (one
  invoice per order, or all of a day's selected lines consolidated onto
  one invoice for that company).
- New Settings > Invoicing section: default VAT rate, next invoice number,
  payment terms, company registration number/email, and optional bank
  details - the bank details box is left off the PDF entirely unless
  actually filled in, never fabricated.
- Local PDF backup: generated invoices/credit notes are saved to a new
  bns_invoices_data Docker volume (not yet covered by backup.sh/restore.sh
  - flagged as a known gap in the changelog).

Login throttling:
- Repeated failed logins for the same IP or the same username now face a
  growing delay (a few free attempts, then doubling up to a 30s cap)
  instead of being retried instantly. Deliberately not a hard lockout -
  mistyping a password can never lock a genuine user out of their own
  account.

Also updates the Setup Guide PDF, README and CHANGELOG for both features.

Note: this environment's Maven Central/npm registry access is blocked, so
none of this has been compiled or type-checked - only manually reviewed.

